=== moe-cache FORK BUILT AND TESTED ON THIS BOX: CANNOT WORK HERE ===
GenerelSchwerz/llama.cpp branch moe-cache (e69cf66), built with the portable
toolchain into src/moecache/build-mc. Loads fine, generates correct text, but:
  --moe-expert-cache-mib 2048 --...-host-pinned-mb 2048   ~1.5 tok/s, disk 148 MB/s
  --moe-expert-cache-mib 6144 --...-host-pinned-mb 18432  1.58 cold -> 1.72
vs 6.70 on the PR fork. Startup refuses ALL 48 layers from the host tier:
  moe-cache-host: admission group=N ... reason=read_only_registration_unsupported cuda=none

ROOT CAUSE (verified with a CUDA probe, scratchpad/probe.cu):
  cudaDevAttrHostRegisterSupported             = 1
  cudaDevAttrHostRegisterReadOnlySupported     = 0   <-- the host tier requires it
  cudaDevAttrPageableMemoryAccess              = 0
  cudaDevAttrCanUseHostPointerForRegisteredMem = 0
moe-cache-host.cu:627 demands cudaDevAttrHostRegisterReadOnlySupported because
--load-mode mmap gives it a READ-ONLY file mapping (moe_cached_buffer_from_host_ptr
wraps those read_only=true). cudaHostRegisterReadOnly does not exist under Windows
WDDM, so the host expert tier - the whole point of the fork - is dead and every
expert page-faults off the mmap. Same pathology already measured as 2x worse here.
Their wiki says Windows needs a special WDDM partial-pinning setup; their issue
#104 is the Windows breakage. This is that limitation, measured.

WHY --load-mode none DOES NOT RESCUE IT: writable host registration IS supported
(attr=1) and the fork has a writable path (llama-model-loader.cpp:1976, read_only=
false, pins fine) - which is why their 12GB profile uses --load-mode none. But it
needs experts in ordinary RAM: 45.29 GiB vs ~27 GiB available, and without mmap the
26.82 GiB PLE table loses its lazy read too. Does not fit. --moe-expert-cache-layers
would leave the unselected layers on the slow mmap-fault path.
=> anndev's 10.8-12.4 needs a non-WDDM platform AND the Gen4 link.

ALSO: --moe-expert-cache-mib and --moe-expert-cache-size are mutually exclusive
("conflicts with a nonzero --moe-expert-cache-size"), and the build needs
cudart64_13/cublas64_13/cublasLt64_13.dll copied into build-mc/bin or it exits
with 0xC0000135 STATUS_DLL_NOT_FOUND.

