=== CACHE WARMING: WORKS, AND IT IS A TIME-TO-FIRST-TOKEN FEATURE ===
LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_HEAT=<path> (+ optional LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_WARM_GB=<n>).
Startup on the second run: "warmed 3216 device slots + 0.00 GiB into the page cache
in 6.7 s" - 3216 = 67 slots x 48 layers, i.e. every slot refilled from the saved
ranking. Both runs cold-cache, every generation measured:
                     cold    preloaded
  1st prefill        2.29 -> 4.46   +95%
  1st decode         5.52 -> 5.86   +6%
  2nd prefill        4.09 -> 4.42   +8%
  2nd decode         7.09 -> 6.98   -2%
  3rd                noise
Prefill touches far more distinct experts per step than decode, so a pre-filled L1
helps it much more. Steady-state decode unchanged, consistent with L1 hit 70->75%
and halving disk reads both measuring as nulls. Enabled in run-full177b.bat.
THREE BUGS had to be fixed first:
 - LRU stamps inverted: reserve_slot_locked bumps slot_last_use, so filling
   hottest-first made the hottest expert the oldest and first to be evicted.
 - route_hotness not restored: eviction ranks by hotness, so a zero-hotness warm set
   was discarded within ~30 tokens. The file stores heat with the ranking for this.
 - destructor-only save never fired: taskkill / window close / crash all use
   TerminateProcess, no destructors. First test showed 7.19 vs 7.22 = two cold runs,
   pure noise. Now checkpointed every ~256 tokens, .tmp + rename so a kill mid-save
   cannot truncate it.
CAVEAT for reporting: that test warmed on the same 8 prompts it measured. For a
published number, warm on one prompt set and measure on another.

