Full run: ctl 8.14 tok/s vs pinned-12 6.95; mean stall over 32 matched states
125.4 -> 152.1 ms (+21.3%). The arena's own hit rate was 55% - it served over half of
every L1 miss from pinned host RAM and STILL lost 21%.

CORRECTION from a pageable arm at the same size - it is the RAM, not the DMA path:
                    tok/s   upload   src med
  control            8.14     37.2    171.7
  pinned-12 (DMA)    6.95     57.9     11.2
  pageable-12 (copy) 6.92     66.8     41.1
Pinned and pageable are IDENTICAL (6.95 vs 6.92), and the pageable arm never DMAs
from the arena yet its upload is higher still. So "DMA out of a big arena is slower"
was WRONG. The whole loss is that 12 GiB taken is 12 GiB the page cache no longer
has: src med 171.7 -> 41.1/11.2, i.e. the arena REPLACED the middle tier instead of
adding to it, and a 55%-hit arena is worth less than the page cache it displaced.

=> EVERY L2 variant loses here: pageable copying (8/12/16/19 GiB), zero-extra-copy,
pinned-staging, pinned-DMA. Not an implementation problem - on 32 GB there is no
spare RAM to build a tier out of. Stop trying host tiers on this box.

